<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 159 0 R
/E (The study revealed that users rely heavily on visual hierarchy, imagery, and layout structure when navigating menus. Menus with excessive options or cluttered layouts tend to create cognitive overload, resulting in confusion and delayed decisions. Highlighted elements such as featured items, boxes, or images act as behavioral nudges, guiding user attention and influencing choices. Additionally, QR-based menus, although convenient, sometimes reduce usability due to navigation complexity, scrolling effort, and limited screen visibility.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
