/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 167 0 R
/E (The analysis highlights that menu design directly influences attention flow, perception, and decision-making efficiency. Visual hierarchy determines how users navigate and prioritize information, while imagery and highlighted elements act as strong attention and decision triggers. Excessive options increase cognitive load and decision fatigue, reducing efficiency, whereas structured and minimal layouts improve clarity, speed, and user confidence. Overall, menu design functions as a behavioral guide, subtly directing user choices.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [3]
>>
