/Title (The research included a set of structured and semi-structured questions aimed at understanding user behavior, perception, and decision triggers. Questions explored factors influencing ordering choices, the role of images and descriptions, ease of navigation, and points of confusion within menus. Users were also asked about their attention patterns, such as what they notice first and whether highlighted or visually emphasized items affect their final selection. These questions helped uncover both conscious and subconscious influences on decision-making.)
